Guards
- stall_weight 0 with rent 0 (room free by the frontier) makes every start cost 0 and read_start returns None
  (nothing beats best_cost = 0): arrival. Wanted: with lateness free no early read pays.
- stall_weight > 0 with rent 0 starts every read at once when r > W. The frontier's price follows evictions with a
  30 s half-life while a staged pin lasts until its turn arrives, so a burst of stagings can overshoot the room
  before lam answers. Bound it with what exists (pin budget 0.3 x pool, NTP_MAX_STAGINGS, NTP_MAX_PARKED) and take
  max(frontier price, the price of the next victim) when deciding a staging: ReturnChanceStrategy.holding_rate of
  the lowest-priority evictable host leaf, 29 to 639 leaves in campaign 34's census, so one heap pass per staging.
- The GPU-bound filter of _queue_ahead (W = whole queue while a ready turn has waited 0.5 s, else 0) stays: it hides
  the read behind the queue; c weighs what is left. With c from the board the filter and the weight move together.
